  "Question": "The value of \\(10^{\\log_{10}7}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\log_{10}7\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\log_7 10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "By definition, \\(\\log_{10}7\\) is the exponent \\(t\\) for which \\(10^t=7\\). The logarithm is defined because its base \\(10\\) is positive and different from \\(1\\), and its argument \\(7\\) is positive. Therefore\n\\[\n10^{\\log_{10}7}=\\boxed{7},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
